Financial holding / Mixed Financial Holding Company defined as follows:
Financial holding company – as defined in point (20) of Article 4(1) of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013;
Mixed financial holding company – as defined in point (21) of Article 4(1) of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013;

Banking Group defined as follows:
-	Member State Level Banking Group – a group of undertakings of which at least one is a credit institution and which consists of a parent undertaking set up in an EEA Member State which is not a subsidiary of an undertaking with a head office in the same Member State (point (16) of Article 4(1) of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013) and which does not fall under the definition of EEA Level Banking Group;
-	EEA Level Banking Group – a group of undertakings of which at least one is a credit institution and which consists of a parent undertaking set up in an EEA Member State and its subsidiaries, or of undertakings linked to each other by a relationship as set out in Article 22 of Directive 2013/34/EU;
